From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: port mali_kbase to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(gpu: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx))

Port private/google-modules/gpu to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
API migrations. Mostly mechanical; entries that change behaviour say so:

  - platform_driver.remove returns void (6.11)
  - del_timer*() renamed timer_delete*() (6.15)
  - MODULE_IMPORT_NS() takes a string literal (6.13)
  - drop in-tree-only include paths that -Wmissing-include-dirs now rejects
  - mali: driver-owned movable pages removed (6.17): page migration forced off,
    __SetPageMovable/__ClearPageMovable stubbed (ACK already defaulted it off)
  - hrtimer_init() + .function replaced by hrtimer_setup() (6.15)
  - dma_fence_ops.fence_value_str removed
  - sscd: driver_override applied at registration (6.18, gs_platform_compat.h)

27 files.

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline (7.3):

  * Kbuild: kbuild no longer appends $(EXTRA_CFLAGS) to compiles, and the
    mali Makefile passes every -DCONFIG_MALI_* switch that way -- so on
    android-mainline they were silently dropped from the C code (first
    visible as trace_mali_pm_*_state being undeclared, because
    CONFIG_MALI_GATOR_SUPPORT vanished; CONFIG_MALI_REAL_HW etc. went with
    it). ccflags-y += $(EXTRA_CFLAGS) restores exactly what kbuild used to do.
  * mm_get_unmapped_area() lost its mm argument (always current->mm, which
    is what kbase passes).
  * shmem_file_setup() takes vma_flags_t: VM_NORESERVE ->
    mk_vma_flags(VMA_NORESERVE_BIT).
  * dma_fence_signal() returns void; the "already signalled" result was
    treated as success anyway.
